"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkmi_sitio=globalThis.webpackChunkmi_sitio||[]).push([[8130],{7735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"brakeza3d-0-26-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-10","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-04-launch-0.26.10-release.md","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.10 released!","description":"Brakeza3D 0.26.10 is here! This release is all about performance and polish: a reworked renderer","date":"2026-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"community","permalink":"/blog/tags/community"}],"readingTime":4.98,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"brakeza3d-0-26-10","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.10 released!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","release","community"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.8 released!","permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-8"}},"content":"Brakeza3D **0.26.10** is here! This release is all about **performance and polish**: a reworked renderer\\r\\nwith instancing and shared GPU geometry, emissive materials, a brand-new audio backend, faster async\\r\\nloading, a much more capable UI system, path costs for pathfinding, and command-line parameters for\\r\\nautomated runs.\\r\\n\\r\\nDownload for **Linux** and **Windows**:\\r\\n- https://github.com/rzeronte/brakeza3d/releases/tag/0.26.10\\r\\n- https://brakeza.com/downloads\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n## \u2728 What\'s New\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Rendering Performance Overhaul\\r\\n\\r\\nThe deferred renderer has been profiled and optimized end to end. Scenes with many copies of the same\\r\\nmodel are now dramatically cheaper.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Shared GPU geometry** \u2014 every `Mesh3D` / `Mesh3DAnimation` created from the same model file shares\\r\\n  its vertex buffers, with deduplicated index buffers\\r\\n- **Instancing** \u2014 an opaque render queue groups objects by model and draws them instanced in the\\r\\n  G-Buffer, shadow and picking passes. Animated models too: bones are skinned in the vertex shader from\\r\\n  a bone-matrix texture buffer\\r\\n- **Shadow caster culling** \u2014 each light only renders the casters inside its own frustum\\r\\n- **State caches** \u2014 FBO/program bind cache and a shared GL render-state cache remove redundant state\\r\\n  changes; projection and view travel in a single `CameraBlock` uniform buffer\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Emissive Materials\\r\\n\\r\\n`Mesh3D` objects can now **glow** with their own color, ignoring scene lighting: screens, neon signs,\\r\\nlamps, magic effects. Emission is off by default and adds no cost to scenes that do not use it.\\r\\n\\r\\n```lua\\r\\nlocal sign = Brakeza:getObjectByName(\\"neon_sign\\")\\r\\nsign:setEmissionEnabled(true)\\r\\nsign:setEmissionIntensity(0.8)   -- 0 = lit normally, 1 = full self-illumination\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAvailable in the object inspector, saved in scene files and fully scriptable.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### New Audio Backend: miniaudio\\r\\n\\r\\nSDL2_mixer has been replaced by **[miniaudio](https://miniaud.io)**, bundled as a single header \u2014\\r\\none dependency less to install on Linux.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Same Lua API as before (`playSound`, channels, `Sound3D`, ambience volume...)\\r\\n- **WAV, MP3 and FLAC** support, also for positional `Sound3D` sources\\r\\n- New `setChannelPitch(channel, pitch)` for engine RPM, Doppler and similar effects\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Faster Async Loading\\r\\n\\r\\n- Per-file load locks in the resource caches: the same file is never loaded twice in parallel\\r\\n- The compute thread pool is sized from the CPU core count\\r\\n- Deferrable jobs: work that has to wait no longer blocks a worker thread\\r\\n- Animated billboards get their own texture cache\\r\\n- `Brakeza:getPendingJobsCount()` and `Brakeza:cancelPendingJobs()` to drive loading screens and\\r\\n  clean restarts; `Components:Render():PreloadImage2D(path)` warms up images before they are shown\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### UI System Upgrades\\r\\n\\r\\nThe widget system takes a big step forward:\\r\\n\\r\\n| Feature | Detail |\\r\\n|---------|--------|\\r\\n| Fonts per widget and per element | Any `.ttf` / `.otf`; nested widgets inherit the parent\'s font |\\r\\n| Word-wrapped text | `wrap`, `w`, `maxLines` and `lineSpacing` on text elements |\\r\\n| 9-slice backgrounds | `bgSlice`: frames whose corners keep their size when the panel is resized |\\r\\n| Scrollable lists | New `scroll` element type |\\r\\n| Pagers on top | `arrayPagerTop` places a long list\'s pager above it |\\r\\n| Resolution-aware text | `setUIDesignResolution(w, h)` and per-widget `refHeight` scale text with the window |\\r\\n| New Lua helpers | `getWidgetSize`, `invalidateWidget`, `invalidateAllWidgets`, `isUIScrollHovered` |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe UI Manager editor window gained the matching controls (font pickers, grouped sections...).\\r\\n\\r\\nRelated rendering helpers:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `drawFillSubmesh(obj, submesh, r, g, b, a)` \u2014 translucent highlight over a single submesh\\r\\n- `TextWriter:measureTextWidthAtlas(text, scale)` \u2014 measure batched atlas text to center or align it;\\r\\n  atlas text now honors its tint color and blends correctly\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Pathfinding \u2014 Path Costs\\r\\n\\r\\n`Grid3D` cells can now have a **traversal cost**. A* prefers cheaper cells, so units can favour\\r\\nsidewalks over roads or avoid dangerous areas without blocking them:\\r\\n\\r\\n```lua\\r\\nlocal grid = mesh:getGrid3D()\\r\\ngrid:fillCostFromImage(\\"../assets/nav/roads.png\\", 128, 4.0)   -- roads cost 4\\r\\ngrid:setCellsCost({ 10, 12, 11, 12 }, 10.0)                   -- a temporary danger zone\\r\\nprint(grid:getCellCost(10, 12))\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nGrid world coordinates are now derived from the grid bounds.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Command-Line Parameters & Automation\\r\\n\\r\\nProjects can declare their own parameters and receive them from the command line \u2014 ideal for test\\r\\nscenarios, CI and benchmarks:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\n> brakeza3d.exe -p MyGame.json --set level=forest --set godMode=true --exit-after 300\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n- `--set key=value` \u2014 passed to the project, declared in its `cli_params` (name, type, default)\\r\\n- `--exit-after N` \u2014 safety watchdog for headless runs\\r\\n- `Brakeza:getCliParam(name)` reads a parameter with its declared type\\r\\n- `Brakeza:requestExit(code)` closes the app with a process exit code\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Scripting API Additions\\r\\n\\r\\n| API | Description |\\r\\n|-----|-------------|\\r\\n| `Brakeza:getDeltaTimeMS()` | Frame time in milliseconds (`getDeltaTimeMicro()` now really returns microseconds) |\\r\\n| `Brakeza:getImage3DAnimationByName()` | Typed access to animated billboards |\\r\\n| `BillboardAnimation:setTowardsCamera / setSize / setRenderFB` | Flat ground sprites, runtime resizing, render layer |\\r\\n| `Mesh3D:getModelFile()` / `getDiffuseTextureFile(i)` | Inspect the model and per-submesh textures |\\r\\n| `Input:isMouseInWindow()` | Know when the cursor leaves the window |\\r\\n| `ParticlesContext.PARTICLE_SIZE_SCALE` | Particle size multiplier |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Profiler \u2014 Render Detail\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Profiler adds exact per-frame **draw call and triangle counters**, CPU and real **GPU time per\\r\\nrender pass** (GPU queries are optional, zero overhead when off), rolling history with median/P95/P99,\\r\\nand **CSV export** to compare a scene before and after an optimization.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Editor & Platform\\r\\n\\r\\n- Scene badge in the project panel\\r\\n- Windows: the application icon is embedded in the executable (taskbar icon from the first frame)\\r\\n- New minimal **UITest** demo scene (`UIWidgetsDemo.lua`) showing a plain widget, a nested widget and an\\r\\n  array with the sample widgets in `assets/ui/`\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Bug Fixes\\r\\n\\r\\n- Texture unit helpers only handled units 0\u20135 (higher units were bound onto the previous one)\\r\\n- UI widget editor now saves `arrayPrefix`\\r\\n- Black scene after a window resize (VAO name reuse in ground decals)\\r\\n- VRAM leak when destroying custom code shaders\\r\\n- Outline fill pass inheriting instancing flags\\r\\n- Editor grid disappearing\\r\\n- Two use-after-free crashes\\r\\n- Camera up vector computed from its own rotation\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n### Documentation\\r\\n\\r\\n- **UI Widgets** \u2014 new dedicated page: JSON format, element types, buttons, nested widgets, lists and\\r\\n  pagination, scroll areas, 9-slice backgrounds, text scaling and the UI Manager editor\\r\\n- **3D Objects** \u2014 Mesh3D model/texture methods, emission, shared geometry and instancing, animated billboards\\r\\n- **Grid3D** \u2014 movement costs\\r\\n- **Scripting introduction** \u2014 command-line parameters (`--set`, `cli_params`, `--exit-after`),\\r\\n  `requestExit`, async loading helpers\\r\\n- **Sound** \u2014 miniaudio backend, supported formats, `setChannelPitch`\\r\\n- **Text System** \u2014 custom fonts with the glyph atlas, batched text and `measureTextWidthAtlas`\\r\\n- **Editor** \u2014 Profiler counters, GPU timing and CSV export\\r\\n- **Download and Install** \u2014 build from source updated: new Windows libraries package for 0.26.10\\r\\n  (no SDL2_mixer, exact MinGW build it needs) and the FFmpeg development packages on Linux\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\nThanks for testing Brakeza3D and sharing feedback \u2764\ufe0f"},{"id":"brakeza3d-0-26-8","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-8","source":"@site/blog/2026-07-31-launch-0.26.8-release.md","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.8 released!","description":"Brakeza3D 0.26.8 is here! This release is packed with major new features: a full positional audio system, multi-scene support, video playback, a new Swarm entity, multi-selection across editor and scripting, and a large batch of rendering, physics, and editor improvements.","date":"2026-07-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"community","permalink":"/blog/tags/community"}],"readingTime":5.19,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"brakeza3d-0-26-8","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.8 released!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","release","community"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.10 released!","permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-10"},"nextItem":{"title":"Thanks and Roadmap!","permalink":"/blog/2026-02-21-thanks-and-road-map"}},"content":"Brakeza3D **0.26.8** is here! This release is packed with major new features: a full positional audio system, multi-scene support, video playback, a new Swarm entity, multi-selection across editor and scripting, and a large batch of rendering, physics, and editor improvements.\\n\\nDownload for **Linux** and **Windows**:\\n- https://github.com/rzeronte/brakeza3d/releases/tag/0.26.8\\n- https://brakeza.com/downloads\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## \u2728 What\'s New\\n---\\n\\n### Sound3D \u2014 Positional Audio System\\n\\nA brand-new `Sound3D` scene object brings distance-based volume attenuation to the engine. Place ambient sounds anywhere in the world and let the engine handle volume falloff automatically based on the camera\'s distance.\\n\\n- Full inner/outer radius model: full volume inside `innerRadius`, linear fade to silence at `outerRadius`\\n- Can be placed in the editor, saved in scene files, or created from Lua with `ObjectFactory.Sound3D()`\\n- **Global ambience volume** \u2014 `Components:Sound():setAmbienceVolume(percent)` scales all `Sound3D` sources simultaneously, perfect for ducking world sounds during menus or cutscenes\\n- Zone music crossfade: overlapping outer radii produce natural transitions with zero scripting\\n- Background music mode: set `innerRadius` to a very large value for a non-positional track\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal snd = ObjectFactory.Sound3D(\\n    \\"../assets/sounds/forest_ambient.wav\\",\\n    Vertex3D.new(0, 0, 0), 20, 80, 100\\n)\\nsnd:setSoundLoop(true)\\nBrakeza:addObject3D(snd, \\"forest_ambient\\")\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Multi-Scene System\\n\\nScenes can now be loaded, shown, and hidden independently at runtime. Multiple scenes can coexist and be toggled without losing their state.\\n\\n- `Brakeza:loadScene(path)` / `Brakeza:showScene(name)` / `Brakeza:hideScene(name)`\\n- Scene shader chains are properly saved and restored when a scene is hidden and re-shown \u2014 shaders that were disabled before hiding stay disabled on restore\\n- Enables interior/exterior streaming: load interior scene, hide exterior, restore on exit\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Video Player in Image2D\\n\\n`Image2D` objects can now play back video files directly inside the engine. Use the editor or Lua to assign a video source and control playback.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Swarm Entity\\n\\nA new `Swarm` object type for managing large groups of simple elements (particles, foliage, crowds) as a single scene node. Registered in the full serialization pipeline with editor inspector support.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Multi-Selection \u2014 Editor & Scripting\\n\\nSelect multiple objects simultaneously in the viewport and operate on them as a group.\\n\\n- **Ctrl + Left Click** \u2014 toggle an object into/out of the current selection group\\n- **Ctrl + Left Drag** \u2014 rectangle-select all objects inside the drawn area\\n- Full scripting access via the new `SelectionManager` (extracted from `ComponentRender`), exposable to Lua\\n- `MultiSelectionDemo.lua` updated with working examples\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Rendering \u2014 Blob Shadows & Ground Circles\\n\\nTwo new lightweight render primitives for real-time ground projection effects:\\n\\n- **Blob shadows** \u2014 circular soft-shadow decals projected onto the ground beneath objects\\n- **Ground circles** \u2014 configurable radius/color rings for selection indicators, AoE zones, and UI feedback\\n\\nBoth are registered as GUI addons and fully scriptable from Lua.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Collider System Improvements\\n\\n- **Debug draw** \u2014 visualize collision shapes in the viewport at runtime\\n- **Contact points** \u2014 query per-frame collision contact data from Lua\\n- `resetColliderRotation()` \u2014 snap a body\'s orientation back to identity without repositioning\\n- Ghost body fix \u2014 ghost objects no longer interfere with dynamic simulation incorrectly\\n- `ColliderGUI` refactored into its own standalone panel\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Shadow Pass Optimization\\n\\nThe shadow pass now skips meshes and scene regions that cannot cast shadows into the current light frustum, reducing GPU draw calls significantly in larger scenes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Editor Improvements\\n\\n| Feature | Detail |\\n|---------|--------|\\n| Solo window toggle | Focus a single dockable panel, hiding the rest |\\n| Layout restore | Layouts are saved and restored across sessions |\\n| `forceReloadLayout` | Force-rebuild the dock layout from the current preset |\\n| `Ctrl + \\\\`` shortcut | Quick toggle between CODING and DEFAULT layouts |\\n| Snap camera views | **Insert** (front), **Home** (top), **Page Up** (side) \u2014 snaps camera to selected object |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### UIManager Improvements\\n\\n- `bgColor` arrays: per-widget background color now accepts RGBA arrays in JSON\\n- `cacheable: false` flag \u2014 bypass FBO caching for widgets that update position or alpha every frame (e.g. world-space unit overlays)\\n- New scripting methods exposed: `setWidgetAlpha`, `setWidgetPosition`, `showWidget`, `hideWidget`, and more\\n\\n---\\n\\n### TextWriter\\n\\n- **Tint color** \u2014 `writeTextAtlasCache` now accepts a tint color parameter, enabling colored cached text without recreating the atlas\\n- `flushTextBatch()` flushes the colored glyph batch correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sound System \u2014 Per-Channel Control\\n\\nNew Lua API for fine-grained channel control:\\n\\n```lua\\n-- Pitch/frequency (engine RPM simulation, Doppler)\\nComponents:Sound():setChannelFrequency(channel, freq)\\n\\n-- Per-channel volume (independent of global setSoundsVolume)\\nComponents:Sound():setChannelVolume(channel, vol)\\n\\n-- 3D spatialization via angle + distance\\nComponents:Sound():setChannelPosition(channel, angle, distance)\\n\\n-- Query channel state\\nComponents:Sound():isChannelPlaying(channel)\\nComponents:Sound():isSoundPlaying(\\"label\\")\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Tools\\n\\n- `fbx_bounds.py` \u2014 Python tool to extract vertex bounds from FBX files, useful for computing exact mesh positions after Blender export\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\nMajor documentation additions:\\n\\n- **Sound3D** \u2014 new dedicated API page covering positional audio, zone crossfade, ambience volume, and Lua methods\\n- **Sound System** \u2014 expanded with per-channel control, `isSoundPlaying`, and `setAmbienceVolume`\\n- **Components API** \u2014 UIManager widget system documented (9 methods)\\n- **3D Objects** \u2014 `Image3DAnimation360` section added\\n- **Shaders System** \u2014 pipeline order and execution steps documented\\n- **Keyboard Shortcuts** \u2014 snap camera keys (Insert / Home / Page Up) added\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Profiler \u2014 Expanded Diagnostics\\n\\nThe built-in ImGui profiler gained a large set of new panels, turning it into a full runtime diagnostics tool:\\n\\n| Panel | What it shows |\\n|-------|---------------|\\n| **Frame Time** | Per-frame ms plot with 120-frame rolling history |\\n| **Components** | Per-component pre/update/post timing breakdown with sparklines |\\n| **Script Detail** | Per-Lua-script timing, toggled independently |\\n| **Caches** | Live entry counts and memory usage for Image, Model, Animation, Script, and Scene caches |\\n| **Frame Buffers** | All active FBOs with their color/depth attachments and dimensions |\\n| **OpenGL Status** | Current GL state: bound program, bound FBO, active texture units, FBO/program switch counters per frame |\\n| **Post-Processing Chain** | Enabled/disabled status and execution order of every scene shader in the chain |\\n| **Thread Pools** | Active tasks, pending tasks, pending callbacks, total processed, and a 120-frame throughput sparkline per pool |\\n| **Colliders** | Runtime list of active physics bodies with mode, group, and AABB |\\n| **System Memory** | Total and free RAM on Windows, Linux, and macOS via native OS APIs |\\n\\nFBO and GL program switch counters are incremented at the call site throughout the render pipeline, giving exact per-frame context switch counts with no estimation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Bug Fixes & Maintenance\\n\\n- Fixed GCC warnings in debug mode across multiple translation units\\n- Fixed X11 + NVIDIA OpenGL window creation on Linux\\n- Fixed `Image2D` size/position regression\\n- Fixed bad `dynamic_cast` in core components\\n- Removed RTS-specific demo widgets from engine examples, keeping only generic ones\\n- Debian build setup scripts updated\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis release marks a significant step forward in audio, scene management, and editor workflow. Thanks for testing Brakeza3D and sharing feedback \u2764\ufe0f"},{"id":"2026-02-21-thanks-and-road-map","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/2026-02-21-thanks-and-road-map","source":"@site/blog/2026-02-21-thanks-and-roadmap.md","title":"Thanks and Roadmap!","description":"First of all, thank you.","date":"2026-02-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"roadmap","permalink":"/blog/tags/roadmap"},{"inline":true,"label":"community","permalink":"/blog/tags/community"}],"readingTime":1.93,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"2026-02-21-thanks-and-road-map","title":"Thanks and Roadmap!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","roadmap","community"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.8 released!","permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-8"},"nextItem":{"title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.2 released!","permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-2"}},"content":"First of all, **thank you**.\\r\\n\\r\\nI want to take a moment to thank everyone who has emailed me and shown so much interest after the latest video about the **Brakeza3D 0.26.2** release. The response from the community has been incredibly positive and motivating, and it truly means a lot to see so many people interested, testing the engine, and asking how they can use it or contribute.\\r\\n\\r\\n## About the roadmap\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of the questions that keeps coming up in messages is:\\r\\n\\r\\n> *What is the project\'s roadmap?*\\r\\n\\r\\nThe answer is clear and honest:  \\r\\n**The current priority is not to add lots of new features, but to stabilize and consolidate the project.**\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main focus right now is:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Stabilizing the engine\\r\\n- Improving internal consistency\\r\\n- Exposing **100% of the engine\u2019s functionality to LUA**\\r\\n- Properly documenting that API\\r\\n\\r\\nAt the moment, the LUA API is still limited, and before expanding the engine with new capabilities, I want to make sure everything that already exists is:\\r\\n\\r\\n- accessible\\r\\n- stable\\r\\n- documented\\r\\n- maintainable\\r\\n\\r\\nThis step is essential to make the project truly usable in the long term.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Priorities for the coming months\\r\\n\\r\\nThe priority order will be:\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **Bug fixing**\\r\\n2. **Documenting the LUA API and the C++ core**\\r\\n3. **Desired features**\\r\\n4. **Long-term features**\\r\\n\\r\\nThis order is intentional. An engine with many features but poor stability or documentation ends up being frustrating for users. I prefer building a solid foundation before accelerating development.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Desired features (mid-term)\\r\\n\\r\\nThese are some improvements planned that will be implemented progressively:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Improve user experience in the interface\\r\\n- Enable geometry streaming for Mesh3D objects\\r\\n- Add a basic version of node-based geometry shaders\\r\\n\\r\\nMany of these ideas come directly from community feedback, which helps a lot when deciding what actually brings value.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Long-term features (or subject to reconsideration)\\r\\n\\r\\nThere are also deeper evolution paths that require analysis and experimentation before any decision is made:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Decouple OpenGL / Create a Vulkan backend\\r\\n- Explore alternative scripting language options\\r\\n- Change the project\'s license type\\r\\n\\r\\nThese decisions affect the architecture, philosophy, and long-term direction of the engine, so they will be evaluated carefully and with community feedback.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Thanks again\\r\\n\\r\\nTo close, I want to repeat the most important thing:  \\r\\n**thank you for the interest, feedback, and support.**\\r\\n\\r\\nThis project keeps moving forward thanks to you.\\r\\n\\r\\nLet\u2019s keep going \ud83d\ude80"},{"id":"brakeza3d-0-26-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-2","source":"@site/blog/2026-02-07-launch-0.26.2-release.md","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.2 released!","description":"Brakeza3D 0.26.2 is now available! \ud83d\ude80","date":"2026-02-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"community","permalink":"/blog/tags/community"}],"readingTime":0.82,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"brakeza3d-0-26-2","title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.2 released!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","release","community"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Thanks and Roadmap!","permalink":"/blog/2026-02-21-thanks-and-road-map"},"nextItem":{"title":"Assets Hub Alpha released!","permalink":"/blog/assets-hub"}},"content":"Brakeza3D **0.26.2** is now available! \ud83d\ude80  \\r\\nThis release focuses on editor usability, shader workflow improvements, scripting enhancements, and major internal cleanup.\\r\\n\\r\\nDownload for **Linux** and **Windows**:  \\r\\n- https://github.com/rzeronte/brakeza3d/releases/tag/0.26.2\\r\\n- https://brakeza.com/downloads\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n## \u2728 What\u2019s New\\r\\n---\\r\\n### Rendering & Shaders\\r\\n- Multiple `Mesh3DShaderChain` fixes\\r\\n- Improved Shader Node Editor processing\\r\\n- New internal texture nodes\\r\\n\\r\\n### Editor & UX\\r\\n- Native toolbar with updated icons and colors\\r\\n- Script/shader editor improvements\\r\\n- Documented shortcuts + \u201cClose all tabs\u201d button\\r\\n- Custom project tree widgets\\r\\n\\r\\n### Assets & Projects\\r\\n- Massive cleanup of scenes and demos\\r\\n- Sound asset integration\\r\\n- Unified file browser (scenes, scripts, projects)\\r\\n- Improved project setup and editable metadata\\r\\n\\r\\n### Scripting & Lua\\r\\n- Bullet functions exposed to Lua\\r\\n- Better ComponentScripting workflow\\r\\n- New tutorials and expanded example scripts\\r\\n- Script-controlled sound volume\\r\\n- New `Clean()` function for selective cleanup\\r\\n\\r\\n### Docs & Maintenance\\r\\n- Continuous documentation updates\\r\\n- Linux CMake fixes\\r\\n- Memory management improvements\\r\\n- ImGui style balancing\\r\\n- Extensive `.gitignore` cleanup\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\nThis release brings a cleaner foundation and a smoother workflow across the engine and editor.\\r\\n\\r\\nThanks to everyone testing Brakeza3D and providing feedback \u2764\ufe0f"},{"id":"assets-hub","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/assets-hub","source":"@site/blog/2026-02-01-assets-hub.md","title":"Assets Hub Alpha released!","description":"Assets Hub Alpha Released \ud83d\ude80","date":"2026-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"assets","permalink":"/blog/tags/assets"},{"inline":true,"label":"hub","permalink":"/blog/tags/hub"},{"inline":true,"label":"community","permalink":"/blog/tags/community"}],"readingTime":1.31,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"assets-hub","title":"Assets Hub Alpha released!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","assets","hub","community"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Brakeza3D 0.26.2 released!","permalink":"/blog/brakeza3d-0-26-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Welcome to Brakeza3D!","permalink":"/blog/welcome"}},"content":"## Assets Hub Alpha Released \ud83d\ude80\\n\\nWe\u2019re excited to announce the **alpha release of Assets Hub**, a new platform designed to expand and strengthen the Brakeza3D ecosystem.\\n\\nAssets Hub is an integrated portal where the community can **share, discover, and reuse scripts and shaders** created by other Brakeza3D users. The main goal is to encourage collaboration, learning, and faster development through high-quality community-driven resources.\\n\\n![Assets Hub](/img/hub/01.png)\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Deep Integration with Brakeza3D\\n\\nAssets Hub is **directly integrated into the Brakeza3D engine**. The engine now includes a built-in client that allows users to:\\n\\n- Log in to their Assets Hub account\\n- Browse community-created assets\\n- Vote and rate resources\\n- Download scripts and shaders created by third parties\\n\\nAll of this happens without leaving the engine, keeping the workflow fast and seamless.\\n\\n## Web Portal for Asset Management\\n\\nAssets Hub is also available as a **web platform** at:\\n\\nhttps://hub.brakeza.com/\\n\\nFrom the web interface, creators can **upload, update, and manage their assets**, making it easy to maintain and showcase their contributions to the community.\\n\\n## Alpha Status\\n\\nAssets Hub is currently in **alpha**, which means it is still under active development. Features, workflows, and APIs may change in the coming weeks as we iterate based on feedback.\\n\\nThis early stage is a great opportunity for the community to test the platform and help shape its future.\\n\\n## Free and Ad-Free\\n\\nAssets Hub is a **free service**, with **no advertisements** and no hidden costs. It is built to support the Brakeza3D community and promote open sharing and collaboration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n![Assets Hub](/img/hub/02.png)"},{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/welcome","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-07-welcome.md","title":"Welcome to Brakeza3D!","description":"The Brakeza3D website has been completely relaunched as a site dedicated to providing solid and up-to-date documentation.","date":"2026-01-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"brakeza3d","permalink":"/blog/tags/brakeza-3-d"},{"inline":true,"label":"news","permalink":"/blog/tags/news"},{"inline":true,"label":"welcome","permalink":"/blog/tags/welcome"}],"readingTime":0.41,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Eduardo","title":"Lead Developer @ Brakeza3D","url":"https://github.com/rzeronte","imageURL":"https://github.com/rzeronte.png","key":"eduardo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Welcome to Brakeza3D!","authors":["eduardo"],"tags":["brakeza3d","news","welcome"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Assets Hub Alpha released!","permalink":"/blog/assets-hub"}},"content":"The **Brakeza3D** website has been completely relaunched as a site dedicated to providing **solid and up-to-date documentation**.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nWe\u2019ve redesigned the website from the ground up to make it easier for developers to find tutorials, API references, download links, and more.  \\n\\nThe goal is to help both new and experienced users get the most out of the Brakeza3D engine efficiently.\\n\\nStay tuned for updates, tutorials, and examples that will guide you in creating amazing 2D and 3D games with Brakeza3D!."}]}}')}}]);